<title>INDIA: Indian forex markets closed for Gandhi anniversary.</title>
<headline>Indian forex markets closed for Gandhi anniversary.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian forex markets were shut on Wednesday for a holiday to mark Mahatma Gandhi's birth anniversary, dealers said.</p>
<p>The markets will reopen on Thursday.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, the rupee ended at 35.64/65 per dollar on Tuesday against the opening quote of 35.68/70 on lack of import demand and good dollar supply, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
